            "review_title": "Review at Khai Minh",
            "review_text": "Tim S\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam194 contributions\n0\nFamily Owned Vegan Restaurant\nAug 2016 • Solo\nKhai Minh is a traditional Vietnamese cafe style restaurant with an extensive vegan menu. There is a menu available in English and the staff speak some English. The menu clearly describes the dishes and there us a good choice of food and drinks. Prices are cheap and the quality is good. Whilst I was there I was the only foreigner and I was made to feel very welcome with the waitress helping me with dipping sauces and she gave me a bottle of sesame seed milk. There is also a range of vegan products sold in the restaurant for home cooking.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten September 1, 2016",
